\section{Active bindings}{
  \if{html}{\out{<div class="r6-active-bindings">}}
  \describe{
    \item{\code{bids}}{The buy side of the order book as a list of named lists with \code{price}, \code{quantity} and \code{orders}, best first, read from UBI on every access.}

    \item{\code{offers}}{The sell side of the order book as a list of named lists with \code{price}, \code{quantity} and \code{orders}, best first, read from UBI on every access.}

    \item{\code{best_bid}}{The highest bid in the order book as a named list with \code{price}, \code{quantity} and \code{orders}, or \code{NULL} when nobody is bidding.}

    \item{\code{best_offer}}{The lowest offer in the order book as a named list with \code{price}, \code{quantity} and \code{orders}, or \code{NULL} when nobody is offering.}

    \item{\code{bid_offer_spread}}{The numeric gap between the best offer and the best bid, measured from one quote, or \code{NULL} when either side is empty.}

    \item{\code{mid_price}}{The numeric price halfway between the best bid and the best offer, from one quote, or \code{NULL} when either side is empty.}

    \item{\code{volume_weighted_average_price}}{Today's numeric volume weighted average price, or \code{NULL} when UBI has none.}

    \item{\code{last_quantity}}{The integer quantity of the last trade, or \code{NULL} when UBI has none.}

    \item{\code{total_traded_volume}}{The integer quantity traded so far today, or \code{NULL} when UBI has none.}

    \item{\code{open_interest}}{The integer open interest of a future or an option, or \code{NULL} when UBI has none.}

    \item{\code{last_trade_time}}{When the last trade happened, as a \code{POSIXct} in India time, or \code{NULL} when UBI has none.}

    \item{\code{parents}}{The synthetic orders and held orders in this instrument that UBI's order engine has not finished, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. A parent is one order the engine was asked for, such as a bracket, a trailing stop or a held limit order, and its legs are the broker orders it placed. This is the only way to see a parent that has placed nothing yet, such as an armed trigger. UBI lists every open parent in the account, so this reads them all and keeps this instrument's own.}

    \item{\code{orders}}{Every one of today's orders in this instrument, whatever its status, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. UBI serves the whole account's order book and has no route for one instrument, so reading this reads the whole book and keeps this instrument's own rows. The book is not merged across brokers, so one order placed at one broker appears once, and the same instrument traded at two brokers gives a row from each. The \code{status} column holds UBI's own upper-case status, one of \code{PENDING}, \code{OPEN}, \code{COMPLETE}, \code{CANCELLED}, \code{REJECTED} or \code{EXPIRED}. An order still waiting in the market is \code{PENDING} at some brokers and \code{OPEN} at others, so \code{open_orders} is the way to ask for those. An order UBI's order engine is still holding has not reached a broker and is not here; it is in \code{parents}.}

    \item{\code{open_orders}}{Today's orders in this instrument that can still be changed, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. An order counts as open while it is waiting in the market, which UBI reports as \code{PENDING} at some brokers and \code{OPEN} at others. Those are the orders \code{modify_order()} and \code{cancel_order()} will accept; every other status is final. An order UBI's order engine is still holding has not reached the market, so it is not here; \code{parents} lists it.}

    \item{\code{completed_orders}}{Today's orders in this instrument that filled in full, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none.}

    \item{\code{rejected_orders}}{Today's orders in this instrument that a broker or the exchange refused, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. The \code{status_message} column holds the reason each one was refused, in the words of whoever refused it.}

    \item{\code{cancelled_orders}}{Today's orders in this instrument that were cancelled, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none.}

    \item{\code{trades}}{Today's trades in this instrument as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. UBI serves the whole account's trade book and has no route for one instrument, so this reads the book and keeps its own rows. One order can produce several trades, and each trade names the order it came from.}

    \item{\code{net_positions}}{The positions held in this instrument now, merged across every broker, as a \code{data.frame} whose \code{pnl} column is a list column, or \code{NULL} when none is held. This is UBI's \code{net} bucket, which counts everything open in this instrument whenever it was opened, as against \code{day_positions}, which counts only today. A position is what a derivative or an intraday trade leaves open, as against a holding, which is a share kept in the demat account and belongs to \code{Equity} instead. UBI merges the brokers' positions by instrument and product, so one instrument gives one row per product it is held under, and no row names a broker.}

    \item{\code{day_positions}}{Today's own positions in this instrument, without what was carried in, as a \code{data.frame}, or \code{NULL} when there are none. This is UBI's \code{day} bucket. It has the same shape as \code{net_positions} and counts only what was opened and closed today, so it is usually empty even when \code{net_positions} is not, because only some brokers report a position on a day basis at all.}

    \item{\code{positions_value}}{The numeric worth of this instrument's open positions at the moment, rounded to two places, or \code{NULL} when none is held or any position has no last price. Each position is counted as its quantity times its last price, and the sign is kept, so a long position adds and a short one subtracts. UBI prices a holding but not a position, so this is worked out here. This counts every position, including those held under \code{margin_trading}, \code{cover} and \code{bracket}, because they are real money even though UBI cannot send an order to close them.}

    \item{\code{positions_pnl}}{What this instrument's positions have made or lost, as a named list with numeric \code{realized}, \code{unrealized} and \code{total}, each rounded to two places, or \code{NULL} when none is held. The realised part is profit already booked by closing some of a position today, and the unrealised part is what is still riding on what remains open. Both are added across every position in this instrument, including those held under \code{margin_trading}, \code{cover} and \code{bracket}.}
  }
  \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
