\subsection{\code{TradeableInstrument$cancel_parent()}}{
  Cancels one of the order engine's parents, with every leg it still has resting at a broker, or one part of a plan.

This is how a synthetic order is stopped and how an order the engine is still holding is cancelled. A position the parent has already opened is not closed.

With \code{part}, only that part of a \code{plan} order is cancelled, named by its path, such as \code{"root.each_fill.children.0"} for a bracket's stop, as the parent's \code{parameters.parts} lists it. A part whose turn has not come is never sent, a part waiting on its trigger is ended at once, and a part that has sent orders sends no more pieces and has each of its resting orders cancelled; the rest of the plan carries on, reacting as it does to that part finishing.

When a broker refuses the cancel of one leg, or its outcome is unknown, UBI answers HTTP 207, which is returned rather than signalled, with the parent's \code{state} as \code{cancelling} rather than \code{cancelled}. The parent no longer acts, and becomes \code{cancelled} once the broker reports that leg finished, so read \code{cancelled_legs} to see which one may still be live, and call this again to retry it.

The examples below, in order:
\itemize{
\item Cancel a held limit buy and print the cancelled parent's state and legs.
\item Show that a parent that has already finished cannot be cancelled a second time.
}
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{TradeableInstrument$cancel_parent(parent_id, part = NULL, dry_run = FALSE)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{parent_id}}{The character \code{parent_id} that \code{place_order()} answered with.}
      \item{\code{part}}{The character path of one part of a plan to cancel, or \code{NULL} to cancel the whole parent.}
      \item{\code{dry_run}}{A logical that is \code{TRUE} to have UBI say what would be cancelled, under \code{resting_legs} for a whole parent or \code{orders} for a part, without cancelling anything.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{BadRequestError} when the parent id or part path is malformed; \code{NotFoundError} when the order engine holds no parent with this id, or the plan has no part at this path; \code{ConflictError} when the parent or part has already finished, or the part is kept whole and has not started, or the parent is not a plan and was given a part; \code{ServiceUnavailableError} when the order engine is not running; \code{OrderOutcomeUnknownError} when the engine did not answer in time; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    A named list with \code{parent_id}, \code{synthetic_type}, \code{state}, \code{intent_id} and \code{cancelled_legs}, one entry per leg with its \code{leg_id}, \code{broker}, \code{order_id}, \code{outcome} and \code{status_message}. A part answers instead with \code{parent_id}, \code{synthetic_type}, \code{part}, its \code{state}, \code{outcome}, \code{status_message}, \code{intent_id} and \code{orders}, where each order says in \code{cancel_accepted} whether its broker accepted the cancel, and HTTP 207 with an \code{outcome} of \code{partial} or \code{rejected} is returned rather than signalled.
  }
  \subsection{Examples}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r example copy">}}
    \preformatted{idea <- Equity$new(exchange = "nse", symbol = "IDEA")
price <- round(idea$last_price * 0.97, 2)
answer <- idea$buy_at_limit_price(price = price, quantity = 1, product = "cnc")
parent_id <- answer[["parent_id"]]

cancelled <- idea$cancel_parent(parent_id)
cat(cancelled[["state"]], cancelled[["synthetic_type"]], "\n")
print(cancelled[["cancelled_legs"]])

idea <- Equity$new(exchange = "nse", symbol = "IDEA")
price <- round(idea$last_price * 0.97, 2)
answer <- idea$buy_at_limit_price(price = price, quantity = 1, product = "cnc")
parent_id <- answer[["parent_id"]]

idea$cancel_parent(parent_id)
tryCatch(
  idea$cancel_parent(parent_id),
  ConflictError = function(error) {
    cat("Refused:", conditionMessage(error), "\n")
  }
)
}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
}

