\subsection{\code{TradeableInstrument$liquidate_position()}}{
  Closes one position in this instrument completely.

UBI reads the position when it sends the order and closes the whole of it, so a long position is sold and a short one is bought back.

Only positions held under \code{cnc}, \code{mis} and \code{nrml} are visible here, for the reason given on \code{add_to_position()}. When no product is named, the positions are read once to find the only one held; when one is named, nothing is read here and UBI reads the positions itself.

The examples below, in order:
\itemize{
\item Buy one Vodafone Idea share intraday and close the whole position, with a limit a per cent below the market because some brokers refuse market orders from an API.
\item Close a short intraday position by buying it back, which UBI works out from the position, with a tag on the closing order.
}
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{TradeableInstrument$liquidate_position(
  product = NULL,
  price = NULL,
  validity = NULL,
  after_market = FALSE,
  tag = NULL
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{product}}{The character product of the position to close, \code{"cnc"}, \code{"mis"} or \code{"nrml"}, or \code{NULL} when only one position is held.}
      \item{\code{price}}{The numeric limit price in rupees, or \code{NULL} to send a market order.}
      \item{\code{validity}}{The character validity, \code{"day"} or \code{"ioc"}, or \code{NULL} to let UBI use \code{"day"}.}
      \item{\code{after_market}}{A logical that is \code{TRUE} to send the order as an after-market order.}
      \item{\code{tag}}{A character label of up to twenty letters and digits for the order, or \code{NULL}.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{PositionError} when no product was named and nothing is held, several positions are held, or the product named is not \code{cnc}, \code{mis} or \code{nrml}; \code{ConflictError} when the product named is not held in this instrument; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    The named list \code{place_order()} returns, holding \code{broker}, \code{order_id}, \code{outcome} and the rest.
  }
  \subsection{Examples}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r example copy">}}
