\subsection{\code{TradeableInstrument$liquidate_all_positions()}}{
  Closes every position this instrument holds, under every product.

The positions are read once to list them, and each is then closed with its own order, which UBI sizes and directs from the position when it sends it. Every one is attempted even when an earlier one fails, so a single refusal does not leave the rest open. A position held under a product UBI cannot send an order for, which is \code{margin_trading}, \code{cover} or \code{bracket}, is reported as ignored rather than passed over in silence, and has to be closed at the broker directly.

The examples below, in order:
\itemize{
\item Buy one Vodafone Idea share intraday, then close every position the share holds, under every product, and print what was done.
\item Sell one share short intraday, close every position the share holds with tagged orders, and list any that could not be closed through UBI.
}
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{TradeableInstrument$liquidate_all_positions(
  price = NULL,
  validity = NULL,
  after_market = FALSE,
  tag = NULL
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{price}}{The numeric limit price in rupees for every order, or \code{NULL} to send market orders.}
      \item{\code{validity}}{The character validity, \code{"day"} or \code{"ioc"}, or \code{NULL} to let UBI use \code{"day"}.}
      \item{\code{after_market}}{A logical that is \code{TRUE} to send the orders as after-market orders.}
      \item{\code{tag}}{A character label of up to twenty letters and digits for the orders, or \code{NULL}.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{BrokerError} when no broker's positions could be read; \code{ServiceUnavailableError} when UBI's positions document is missing or too old to serve; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass when the positions could not be read for any other reason. A failure to close one position is reported in the frame instead.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    A \code{data.frame} with one row per position, holding \code{product}, \code{order_product}, \code{quantity}, \code{closed}, \code{order_id} and \code{error}, or \code{NULL} when this instrument holds no position at all.
  }
  \subsection{Examples}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r example copy">}}
